From bd759cce46983faddc7ba46166730b34aece1414 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: LNPANDY <lnp-andy@hotmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 00:59:17 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] The layout editor: long-press the layout button and drag
 every control where it fits
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Each game is its own app, so its layout is its own: a long press on the layout button opens the editor, where every movable control (left stick, A, B, X, Y each on their own, D-pad, shoulders, L3 / R3, − / +) shows a dashed outline to drag anywhere on screen; a one-tap reset at the bottom centre or a long press on the button restores every position. Positions are kept in NSUserDefaults per game as screen fractions, and a control without one sits exactly where the built-in layout puts it. The drawn key, the touch hit-test and the editor's grab read the same place (facePos: and the group anchors), so a moved key cannot trigger at its old spot. The editor holds no game input and the choice survives updates like the layout choice does.

Upstream-Status: pending
Reason: Players ask to place the virtual controls themselves; per-key face buttons, a one-tap reset, and the touch hit-test reading the drawn position (owner-verified on a device)
Issue: LNPANDY/NX2Apple (owner request, virtual pad customization)

